    "size": 20892858,
    "mandatory": false,
    "changelog": "Hotfix over 6.0.\n\nFixed\n- Data loss when upgrading from installs older than 4.5R: the check before deleting the old chroot could miss a still-attached bind and delete through it into internal storage. Detection now covers every layout, and no recursive delete runs while anything is mounted.\n- The install no longer continues after a failed cleanup.\n- Devices without root reported \"no usable tar\" instead of naming the real cause. The pre-check now offers the rootless engine rather than starting an install that cannot finish.\n- Captured handshakes were not moved into the captured folder.\n- Wordlists were not listed in the pickers.\n- The terminal could crash on launch with \"Cannot create component config directory\"."
  },
  "news": [
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Stryker 6.0 - Rootless engine & Debian",
      "description": "The full toolset now runs without root: Stryker boots an arm64 QEMU virtual machine and routes tools into the guest. The chroot moved from Alpine to Debian trixie, the same rootfs the VM boots. Also new: a root-free network scanner (mDNS, SSDP, NetBIOS, SNMP), Cameradar RTSP discovery, a reworked dashboard and VM settings. RouterScan has been removed. arm64-v8a only.",
